>> title: Charred Broccoli, Air Fryer
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: broccoli, air fryer, basket, side, lemon
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: charred-broccoli
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: air fryer broccoli, basket broccoli, air fried broccoli, roasted broccoli in the air fryer
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: narrow — the florets char a good two minutes before the stems soften, so the whole dish is decided by how evenly it was cut
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
Cut evenly. The florets char first and the stems will not catch up.

>> step: cut into even florets, toss with equal parts water and oil
Cut @broccoli{1%lb}(450 g; crowns and peeled stalks) into even florets and toss in a #bowl{} with @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @water{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @kosher salt{1%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 175°C (350°F), 8–12 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)wetted florets{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 175°C (350°F) for ~air fry{10%min}, one layer.

>> step: toss at halfway — the water has gone and the edges are just browning
Toss @&(~1)broccoli{} once.

>> step: toss hot in the same bowl
Toss @&(~1)charred broccoli{} with @garlic{2%cloves}(grated), @lemon zest{1%tsp}, @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @red chile flakes{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: Equal parts water and oil: the water steams the floret soft, and once it has boiled off the oil browns it.
Two stages in one toss. It is why basket vegetables need not come out dry.
